      "location": "Example; Verification 3.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The function and every partial sum are one-periodic, but the item claims at every noninteger real x that the limit is x-1/2. At x=3/2, its displayed partial-sum formula gives S_N f(3/2)=-sum_{k=1}^N sin(3pi k)/(pi k)=0 for every N, whereas the asserted limit is 1. The correct value must use the fractional part of x.",
